                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A direct upgrade from the original Spartan Assault. More weapons, vehicles, enemies (Prometheans), etc. This time the story takes place after the events of Halo 4 and I find it to be a little bit stronger compared to the first one. Probably what helps is the fact that you have a handler that guides you through the missions. She's a little generic, but she reminds me a little of how Cortana works in the original games: someone to keep you company and call out objectives. The missions are much longer than before and I think this was a great change. The original had these short ass levels that were literally five minutes long sometimes. This time around, you're spending at least ten minutes and it feels like an actual mission.\r\n\r\nAchievements are more difficult compared to the original. The Vidmaster ones make an return, but this time there are five and they do not mess around. I would recommend looking up a guide for some as they can be quite tricky, especially the one where you cannot get hit by the beam turrets.\r\n\r\nLast thing: The soundtrack is surprisingly great. You wouldn't expect that from a game like this, but multiple times I found myself saying, \"Damn I need to look up this song later\" while playing. Bravo.\r\n\r\nI got this one super cheap in a bundle with Spartan Assault for $1.24 and it's definitely worth that price. I'd say it's even worth the original price with the amount of content present. If you're a fan of Halo, this one is for you.",
